;;;; Importing lib/parsi/parsi.cicili WITHOUT a prefix
;;;;
;;;; Its pair is example/parsi-prefixed.cicili -- the same page, one line
;;;; different:
;;;;
;;;;   (import "lib/parsi/parsi.cicili" :parsi "demo")   ->  (parsi.PAGE …)
;;;;   (import "lib/parsi/parsi.cicili" nil    "site")   ->  (PAGE …)
;;;;
;;;; NIL IS HOW YOU SAY "NAMESPACE, NO PREFIX". The second argument is the
;;;; prefix and the third is the namespace, and they are independent -- so a
;;;; file can have the plain names and still have its objects qualified. Leave
;;;; the third out as well and the page is simply `hello', served at /hello.zt.
;;;;
;;;; This works because the library declares its own package rather than taking
;;;; the one an importer would have made for it, and read-file evaluates that
;;;; DEFPACKAGE as it reads. Without it, an unprefixed import had nowhere to put
;;;; the definitions.
;;;;
;;;; WHAT IT COSTS, and it is worth knowing before choosing this form:
;;;;
;;;; 1. FOUR MACROS ARE UNREACHABLE. CLASS, TYPE and SEQUENCE belong to
;;;;    COMMON-LISP and ENUM to SB-ALIEN. An object is built by a form Common
;;;;    Lisp evaluates, and CL:EVAL resolves a name by symbol identity rather
;;;;    than through the name-keyed table Cicili dispatches a target's forms
;;;;    through -- so those four cannot be interned here to be found. Written
;;;;    unprefixed,
;;;;
;;;;        (DEFPARAMETER *c* (CLASS holder (PUBLIC)))
;;;;
;;;;    stops with `The variable holder is unbound', because CLASS was read as
;;;;    Common Lisp's own symbol and the form was taken for a function call.
;;;;    A file with a CLASS in it wants the prefixed form. This one has none.
;;;;
;;;; 2. THE NAMES ARE GLOBAL. Registered bare, PAGE, TABLE and SELECT are these
;;;;    macros for every Cicili file compiled in the same process.
;;;;
;;;; So: this form for a file of pages, the prefixed form for anything holding a
;;;; model.
;;;;
;;;; Run:
;;;;   sbcl --script cicili.lisp example/parsi-unprefixed.cicili
;;;;   cp example/site_hello.hpp example/site_hello.cpp $ZIGURATIP_HOME/ld/
;;;;   rm -f $ZIGURATIP_HOME/tmp/site_hello.hpp $ZIGURATIP_HOME/tmp/site_hello.cpp
;;;;   parsi example/hello-bare.parsi
;;;; then http://localhost:2190/site/hello.zt

(import "lib/parsi/parsi.cicili" nil "site")

(DEFPARAMETER *hello*
  (PAGE hello
    (PUBLIC)
    (PAGE_LOAD
      (ECHO "<h1>no prefix</h1>")

      ;; the escape to Cicili -- lifted into site_hello.cpp and called from here
      (ECHO "<p>from Cicili: " (cicili (+ 20 22)) "</p>"))))

;;; Named after the page, the same as in the prefixed file: site::hello lifts
;;; into site_hello.hpp and site_hello.cpp.
(header "site_hello.hpp"  (make :cpp #t) (HPP  *hello*))
(source "site_hello.cpp"  (make :cpp #t) (CPP  *hello*))
(header "hello-bare.parsi" (make :cpp #t) (FILE *hello*))
